From 878808e54f5f2d8209ba7c7edbd66e66a128031a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: c03rad0r <c03rad0r@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 14:24:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] feat(tollwallet): sidecar wallet backend + capability
 manifests

Adds a WalletPort implementation backed by a separate wallet daemon over an
AF_UNIX socket (newline-JSON RPC), so the router can choose its Cashu wallet
backend at runtime without CGO and without linking a Cashu library into the
service. Includes a capability-manifest type (what a backend advertises: kind,
arches, sizes, storage model, contract coverage, licence) used by the sidecar
'info' handshake and by per-target selection tooling.

- sidecar.go: full WalletPort over the RPC (all 15 methods), reconnect-once,
  Token over the wire; stdlib only.
- manifest.go: dependency-free JSON capability manifest + loader.
- manifests/{gonuts,cdk,nucula}.json: the three backends' measured capabilities.
- tests: in-process fake daemon over a temp unix socket; contract, error
  propagation, unreachable; manifest load/validation.

No existing behaviour changes; additive. Design + measurements:
research/wallet-migration (05-architecture/wallet-selection.md,
experiments/cdk-footprint, experiments/nucula-port).
